This product includes software derived from the `zeta23/` project of
anthropics/formal-math (https://github.com/anthropics/formal-math), Copyright (c) 2026
Anthropic, PBC, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0. The derived files are the
ones under `Vendored/Zeta23/`. They have been adapted to this repository's Mathlib version
and pruned at declaration granularity to the dependencies of the unconditional results.
Some surviving proof scripts are simplified to avoid otherwise unused helper lemmas. The
vendored subset consists of the classical analytic inputs of
that project (the Riemann--von Mangoldt formula and local zero count, Weil's explicit formula,
the Montgomery--Vaughan Hilbert inequality, Stirling-type facts for Gamma'/Gamma, the
Chebyshev--Mertens prime sums, and the reflection symmetry of zero multiplicities), together
with the spectral-calculus and zero-tail helpers needed by those inputs. The headline
rank--trace / Gram-matrix argument is not imported. See `Vendored/Zeta23.lean`.

Some of those files (under `Vendored/Zeta23/FromPNTPlus/`) in turn derive from
PrimeNumberTheoremAnd (https://github.com/AlexKontorovich/PrimeNumberTheoremAnd), Copyright
the PrimeNumberTheoremAnd contributors, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; each
carries its upstream notice. Some of those in turn derive from mathlib
(https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4), Copyright the mathlib contributors,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The additional source files under `Vendored/ErdosProblems/Erdos421/` come from
plby/lean-proofs (https://github.com/plby/lean-proofs), commit
87b073cb8b00ffdd32cc6b84e89a7d9fcc6290fe, in `src/latest/ErdosProblems/Erdos421/`.
The included declarations are pruned from the source dependency closure of
`Erdos421.riemannZeta_eventually_ne_zero_log_power_strip`. This theorem concerns
Mathlib's Riemann zeta function and supplies the unconditional zero-free width
c / (log |t|)^(15/16) used at the closed pair-correlation endpoint. The upstream
`src/latest/LICENSE` notice is preserved verbatim in `Vendored/ErdosProblems/LICENSE`; the Lean
sources carry Mathlib-compatibility edits and have unused declarations removed.

The pair-correlation development under `ZetaZeros/Unconditional/` and the
Riemann--von Mangoldt bridge in `ZetaZeros/Zeta/RiemannVonMangoldt.lean` were ported from
AxiomMath/ZetaZerosInternalOld (https://github.com/AxiomMath/ZetaZerosInternalOld),
commit 6303d1a5e42d316674b0133b9cbd80956e592d89. That repository is an immediate source,
not a claim of exclusive authorship: the individual files preserve their contributor
and copyright notices, including Anthropic notices where present. These files are also
pruned to the proof dependencies; `ZetaZeros/Unconditional.lean` supplies the V2 wrappers.
